// Unroll fully unrolls loops that run a small constant number of times,
// so that the copies of the body see their induction variables as
// constants: addresses become fixed offsets that memopt can tell apart,
// inner loops get constant bounds and are unrolled in turn, and the loop
// overhead disappears.
//
// A loop qualifies when its header tests i < n or i <= n, where the phi i
// starts at a constant and steps by a positive constant and n is a
// constant; its only exit is the header's false branch; and the unrolled
// copies fit the size budget. Each copy of the header becomes a jump into
// that iteration's copy of the body, and the last one jumps to the exit.
func Unroll(f *ssa.Func) {
